{"author":{"id":"86dc3c885e4fa466d19699d4a5e74c240f1c9d6b23f4e62ea2d2d8e359bd1711"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789490277,"nonce":"mRDhg0jeRlynd2ql91vAxXsBv60=","title":"Persist and relate tutor sessions","message":"## Parent\n\ngit-bug issue `60b2077` — PRD: GIC v0.9 workshop environment\n\n## What to build\n\nPersist transparent local tutor conversations as append-only JSONL and expose create, resume, rename, compact, and sketch-relationship workflows. Current source and diagnostics remain ephemeral request context rather than repeated session entries.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] The first student question supplies the default session name and the student can rename it.\n- [ ] Session metadata includes creation time, related sketch identity, provider/model changes, and conversation entries.\n- [ ] Restart lists and resumes valid sessions while recovering safely from a partially written final line.\n- [ ] Current source, diagnostics, runtime failure, and output snapshots are injected per request but not duplicated into session history.\n- [ ] Compaction appends summary checkpoints while preserving complete prior JSONL entries.\n- [ ] Renaming a sketch inside GIC updates its relationship; continuing with another sketch clones the session and preserves the original.\n- [ ] Save As, moved, missing, deleted, and unsaved/PWA-style document identities follow one documented relationship policy.\n- [ ] Integration tests use real temporary session files and deterministic tutor exchanges.\n\n## Blocked by\n\n- git-bug issue `cab1222` — Add immutable examples and private recovery\n- git-bug issue `9a74751` — Add native desktop document workflows\n- git-bug issue `39802c0` — Add the deterministic Socratic tutor","files":null}]}